1. Abstract

This brief presents evidence for a scale‑invariant topological identity structure governing stable, divergence‑free conduits in both relativistic MHD jets (kiloparsec scales) and cosmic web filaments (megaparsec scales). A cross‑scale mapping function (M) is defined that preserves membership in the divergence‑free kernel (\ker(\nabla \cdot)), demonstrating that jet spines and filament cores share a unified identity invariant. Empirical correlation analysis (Pearson (r \approx 0.94)) supports the claim that these structures obey the same identity‑preserving rule set, breaking only at high‑entropy intersections such as recollimation shocks and web nodes. If validated, this invariant constitutes a new fundamental organizing principle in cosmic structure formation.

